# ripgrep config - managed by the bootstrap on every platform.
#
# ripgrep reads no config file unless RIPGREP_CONFIG_PATH names one, so the zsh
# fragment and profile.ps1 export it, and only when this file is in place. The
# shells alias grep to rg, so these flags apply to grep at the prompt too
# (except --max-columns: the alias turns it off, as grep never cuts a line).
# Deployed to ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-~/.config}/ripgrep/config on Linux and macOS
# and %APPDATA%\ripgrep\config on Windows. One flag per line, as rg wants.
#
# Every flag here has an opposite for a one-off: --case-sensitive,
# --no-hidden, --max-columns=0. `rg --no-config` drops the whole file.

# Case-insensitive unless the pattern has a capital letter.
--smart-case

# Search dotfiles and dot-directories (.github, .env, .config), the same reach
# the fzf file widgets have. .gitignore is still honoured.
--hidden

# .git itself is only noise once --hidden is on.
--glob=!.git/

# A minified bundle or a lockfile line no longer fills the screen: long lines
# show their first 200 columns, followed by a count of the matches cut off.
--max-columns=200
--max-columns-preview
